{"ts":"2026-11-15T01:06:16.276Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"All claims from NASA Science (published 9 Nov 2026). Launched 13 Nov 2025 with Earth and Mars on opposite sides of the Sun ('a year ago' at posting on 25 Nov 2026); loitered around L2, about a million miles (1.6 million km). Powered flybys on 7 and 9 Nov 2026 ('this month' holds at posting), with about 9-minute burns; the second at about 650 miles, converted to about 1,000 km (1,046). A 10-month cruise; orbit insertion planned for 7 and 9 Sept 2027; formation flying to study solar wind and atmospheric loss. 'First science mission to choreograph two orbiters around Mars' is the PI's quote, attributed to NASA / UC Berkeley. Images are real photos: the NG-2 launch, the ESCAPADE spacecraft in the clean room, and Viking's Mars."},"gitSha":"910e1db"}
